      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 6629bae8bcbe67bce055febc3e79a83182037b43\nparent a527a0077a0fcae913188410214efe98021c0cca\nauthor Jaromil <jaromil@dyne.org> 1794666854 +0100\ncommitter Jaromil <jaromil@dyne.org> 1794675959 +0100\n\nwallet: Clear streams before advancing BDB cursor\n\nLoadRecords reuses its key and value streams between cursor calls. Record\nloaders may leave optional suffix fields unread, which BerkeleyROCursor\ncurrently appends to the next record. This can cause valid legacy wallets\nto fail migration with a deserialization error.\n\nClear both streams before writing the next record, matching SQLiteCursor.\nDocument the cursor's replacement contract, add a BerkeleyRO regression\nthat leaves part of both streams unread, and reuse unread streams in the\nSQLite prefix tests to cover the same contract.\n",
